            <ArticleTitle>Cardiovascular mortality in transient ischemic attacks.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>252-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Statistical analyses were made of the mortality of persons diagnosed as having definite TIA in an epidemiologic survey of a biracial Southern community. None of the usual risk factors associated with this illness such as heart disease, hypertension or diabetes appears to account for the excess deaths observed in a 10 year period of follow up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
